# AWPTCM-T33362 (201) Authentication&Security_DynamicVlan - Multiple Dynamic VLAN (Un-tag)
# Working log, run 1 -- tb277 / swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) -- group B, authmodes-2026-10-23T1304
# Tester: bench-runner subagent, 2026-10-23 16:12-16:26 NZDT (03:12-03:26 UTC)

## What the case asks, and how it was measured

No authored steps in `ck.db`. TPS row **199 "Multiple Dynamic VLAN(Un-tag)" reads `Yes`**. The
dispatch set the objective: *two supplicants on the SAME port receiving DIFFERENT
RADIUS-assigned VLANs, untagged. Prove the VLAN assignment in the dataplane, not only in
`show auth supplicant`.*

That is exactly what is below. The headline is a **2 x 2 dataplane matrix** in which each
supplicant can reach the gateway of its own assigned VLAN and **not** the other's, taken with
`tools/arpleg.py` on the wire; `show auth supplicant` and `show vlan brief` are second witnesses,
and the DUT's own log a third.

