## STEP 2 -- the DISCRIMINATOR: `type single` refuses the second, different VLAN

The one change that distinguishes "Multiple Dynamic VLAN" from ordinary dynamic VLAN assignment.

```
configure terminal / interface port1.0.48 / auth dynamic-vlan-creation type single / end
show auth interface port1.0.48 | include dynamicVlan   ->   dynamicVlanCreation: single-dynamic-vlan
```

Run twice, the second time with ckdv2 declared `--expect failure` so the instrument states the
outcome. Both runs are identical in shape:

